+# Aegis Optimization Pipeline (overview)
+
+This patch provides end-to-end building blocks for:
+ - QAT (quantization-aware training) -> exports quantized candidate
+ - PTQ (post-training quantization) for ONNX
+ - ONNX -> TensorRT engine conversion (FP16/INT8)
+ - DeepSpeed / FSDP training template for large models
+ - CI workflow that runs quantize->convert->canary validate and blocks promotion on regressions
+ - Autoscaling HPA sample using GPU utilization custom metrics (Prometheus adapter)
+ - Adaptive batcher and triton dynamic batch tuner
+ - Node-local model cache prefetcher with LRU eviction
+
+How to use:
+ - Update placeholders to your real models, data paths, S3/GCS URIs and container images.
+ - Ensure trtexec & TensorRT available in CI runners (or skip engine build).
+ - Wire Prometheus adapter to expose GPU metrics as custom metrics for HPA.
+ - Integrate the suggestions from `trace_analyzer.py` and `auto_batch_tuner.py` into your runtime configmaps via GitOps/Argo.
+
+Safety notes:
+ - Always run quantized candidates through safety & red-team tests in canary before promotion.
+ - For INT8 calibration, supply a representative calibration dataset.
+ - DeepSpeed jobs should be run in a controlled environment with proper resource quotas.
